In the early game I like to stay on level N until I reach XP N + 1.
As soon as I find any down stairs I go down as soon as my pet
won't follow me.  I look around to see if it's a regular level or the
mines, then return to explore.

As soon as I'm XP 2 I figure I'm ready to explore level 2.  XP 3,
explore level 3 and so on.  Only for the main dungeon not the
mines.

This strategy on my part suggests that once I find the entrance
to the mines, I wait until I have 1 more XP level, then explore
1 level down in the regular dungeon and also 1 level down in the
mines.  Then with 1 more XP level after that 1 more level in the
main dungoen and 1 more in the mines.  And so on until XP levels
stop coming as regularly.  I end up around 8 or 9 before finishing
mines end doing this.

By the time I've finished the mines and Sokoban XP levels from
killing monsters comes slow enough that I no long wait for XP
levels to go deeper.  I just stay somewhat cautious and stay
ready to run up the stairs when I get in trouble.



